###-*- Mode: Change-Log; coding: utf-8; -*-

v2.1.12-pre1 WIP
	* fixed type of CConcXml::m_Dates (was: vector<int>, new: vector<DWORD>) - should improve portability
	* added doc/ddc_files.pod (-> manpage ddc_files(5)): low-level index file formats
	* started work on using mmap() for runtime index access
	  - added template class ddcMMap<T> in src/CommonLib/ddcMMap.h    : basic mmap() support
	  - added template class ddcVecFile<T> in src/CommonLib/ddcMMap.h : high-level wrapper for slurp or mmap
	  - added opt-file option "MemoryMap" (Boolean)
	  - updated CIndexSetForLoadingStage::m_StringBuffer (vector<char> -> ddcVecFile<char>)
	  - updated CIndexSetForQueryingStage::m_Index (vector<CIndexItem> -> ddcVecFile<CIndexItem>)

v2.1.11 Tue, 20 Mar 2018 13:10:10 +0100 moocow
	* fixed catastrophic error in NavHintKey::operator<() leading to cache inconsistency and random server crashes
	* added server option NavCacheStep: minimum offset increment for navigation cache update
	* CDDCServer now counts 'expand_terms' requests as 'queries' for statistics tracking

v2.1.10 Wed, 14 Mar 2018 14:43:26 +0100 moocow
	* fixed catastrophic typo causing bogus count-query results from branch server
	* fixed inconsistent navigation hint generation if all hits were trimmed (requires 'vacuous' get_hit_strings requests)
	* disabled "vacuous get_hit_strings request" check introduced in v2.0.31
	  - unable to reproduce any noticeable turnaround delay using bz, bz_pp, or bz_meta on kira
	  - allowing vacuous 'get_hit_strings' requests was in fact often faster than without (but only by ca. 1ms in fs-cached case)
	  - dominant factor for query time is fs-cache presence of get_hit_strings *results* (doesn't apply to empty get_hit_strings requests)
	    + fscache @ ca. 10 ms/q ; -fscache @ 430 ms/q
	  - for v2.1.10, we need get_hit_strings even for "empty" daughter result-sets in order to update navigation hints
	* disabled trimming of CFirstHitsQueryResult::m_Hits[] in BranchServer.cpp
	  - we're paying for the memory anyways, and we need all retrieved hits in FHResult for consistent hints (in some cases)
	* refactored navigation cache insertion into new method CDDCBranchServer::UpdateNavCache()

v2.1.9 Thu, 08 Mar 2018 15:51:33 +0100 moocow
	* IndexSet.cpp lookup routines now throw an exception if MaxRegexpExpansionSize is exceeded
	  - misleading old behavior just considered only the first MaxRegexpExpansionSize expansions
	  - there is still no way to get non-fatal warnings passed through to the user via ddc_daemon protocol
	* added support for full-depth "navigation hints" in ConcordLib/NavHint.(cpp|h)
	  - NavHint: encodes local offset, all direct or indirect subcorpus offsets, and sort-key lower bound
	  - NavHintKey: key for NavHintCache (query string + logical hit offset lower bound)
	  - NavHintCache: lockable LRUCache<NavHintKey,NavHint>
	* bandwidth & memory optimizations (mantis bugs #662 and #24816)
	  - leaf: added result-set front-trimming in CConcSession::GetHits()/3
	    + track number of trimmed hits in CConcSession::m_ResultOffset
	  - leaf: added period-wise result-set front-trimming in CConcSession::GetAllHits()/3
	    + not for count queries
	    + use new CConcSession::m_ResultMinKey as a lower-bound hint in the presence of a non-trivial sort operator
	    + added CConcSession::SortKeyLB() to backtranslate from string sort-keys to integers
	    + added cruft template my_upper_bound() in CConcSession.cpp for trimming over descending sorts
	  - leaf: improved period-wise back-trimming in CConcSession::GetAllHits()/3
	    + use new CConcSession::m_ResultOffset and maybe even m_Hits.size() if applicable
	  - branch: added shared NavHintCache (LRU, default size=512)
	    + not for count queries
	    + track lower-bound hints for high-offset "paging" (assuming basically linear progression)
	  - request protocol: added optional HINT (NavHint) parameter to 'get_first_hits' and 'run_query' requests
	    + not used by count queries
	    + branch servers prefer user-supplied HINT if specified, otherwise attempts to use new server m_pNavCache
	  - response protocol: added HINT component to 'get_hit_strings' and 'run_query' JSON output
	    + propagate nested subcorpus offsets to ancestor branches, for cache maintainence and optional user hinting
	* re-worked ddcConfigNoAuto.h generation a la gfsm (safer)
	* added "get_first_hits", "ddc_close_socket" to branch-server m_noLogCommands for log-level < debug
	  - should greatly reduce log verbosity for "deep" branching server-trees
	* disabled DDC_COUNT_KEY_COMPAT hacks introduced for ddc v2.0.38 transition (2015-05-20)
	* update EndHitNo as output parameter in CConcSession::GetAllHits
	  - fixes protocol bug "get_first_hits always returns HITUB=0"
	  - needed for correct NavCache maintainence
	* added server option VersionCompat
	  - really "transmission compatibility": influences messages *sent* by server to clients, daughters
          - required e.g. for dwds c4 corpus, whose daughters would choke on HINTs
	* added server option NavCacheSize

v2.1.8 Fri, 02 Feb 2018 15:06:55 +0100 moocow
	* added UNIX socket support for CCurl and TxCab classes
	  - uses CURLOPT_UNIX_SOCKET_PATH (libcurl >= v7.40.0) by default avaialble
	  - added application-level support for UNIX sockets for libcurl >= 7.21.0 (--enable-curl-unix-sockets)
	  - supported URL formats (--enable-curl-curl-unix-urls):
	    + "http:/path/to/unix/socket//uri/path"        (perl LWP::Protocol::http::SocketUnixAlt style)
	    + "unix:/path/to/unix/socket|http:///uri/path" (apache mod_proxy style)
	    + "http+unix:/path/to/unix/socket//uri/path"   (native http+unix scheme, //-separated)
	    + "http+unix:/path/to/unix/socket|/uri/path"   (native http+unix scheme, |-separated)
	* changed server 'status' memory reporting again
	  - VmRSS is now once again returned as 'memkb' key (but really in kB)
	  - VmSize and other data are parsed from /proc/PID/status (rather than /proc/PID/statm as before)
	  - detailed memory usage is now returned in status 'vmem' key
	* fixes for flex v2.6.1

v2.1.7 Wed, 10 Jan 2018 10:33:26 +0100 moocow
	* changed memory size reporting in ConcordDmnLib/Server.cpp
	  - fixed reporting unit: was pages a la /proc/PID/statm; now: kB (1024-byte units)
	  - formerly reported resident set size (VmRSS), now report total program size (VmSize)
	* fixed ClearString() in utilit.h, which wasn't properly clearing target string capacity as advertised
	  - may contribute to memory bloat in "public" metacorpus server after high-offset result pages (e.g. -start=300000);
	    but simulation on workstation did NOT reproduce any memory bloat symptoms!
	  - also altered ClearVector() correspondingly (even though it WAS still operating as advertised)

