v2.1.1 Thu, 02 Mar 2017 10:25:11 +0100 moocow
	* lexer/parser tweaks for mantis bug #19051
	  - (6er)->('6er) vs. (6-er)->('6' && 'er'), also "2+4-Vertrag"
	  - allowing hypen- and digit-initial symbols wonks up count(...) #by[$w=1-1] , #by[$w-1], etc.
	  - workaround handles index-names specially in lexer (new token-type INDEX)
	    ~ whitespace between '$' and rest of index-name is no longer allowed
	    ~ new non-exclusive lexer state Q_MATCHID used to disable bareword symbols after matchid
	* added server option "StatsWindow" : moving average window size
	* added "qtavg" entry to 'status' response: average query time over last $StatsWindow seconds
	* added CDDCServer::m_SessionStats : track stats for local session
	  - serial mode: session stats added to server-wide m_ServerStats in CDDCServer::HandleClientConnection()
	  - client-thrads: session stats added to parent m_ServerStats in CDDCServerThread::run()
	* factored out CDDCServerStats & co. from ddcServer.(h|cpp) to new ddcServerStats.(h|cpp)
	* split DDCTime into DDCTimeUnix (1 second resolution) + DDCTimeHiRes (1 nanosecond resolution)
	  - generic wrapper typedef DDCTime respects config macro DDC_USE_HIRES_CLOCK
	* renamed "#(ASC|DESC)_CONTEXT" -> "#(ASC|DESC)_MIDDLE" in ConcCommon.h HitSortEnumStrings
	  - CQFContextSort::toString() was returning bogus (unparseable) query strings

v2.1.0 Tue, 03 Jan 2017 12:04:49 +0100 moocow
	* added optional per-client threads for ddc_daemon
	  - each CDDCServer instance can now pre-spawn user-specified N worker threads (NumThreads)
	  - new ddcThread.*, ddcThreadQueue.*, ServerThread.*, new class ddcLockable
	  - added local locks in "unsafe" shared objects: CCurl, CConcXml, CIndexSetForQueryingStage
	    + wrap dangerous locked index sub-object code in try/catch to avoid deadlocks on weird exceptions (e.g. std::bad_alloc)
	* refactored old ConcHolder.* into ConcSessionContext.*, ConcSession.*
	  - ConcSessionContext: shared global data (cache)
	  - ConcSession: thread-local data (everything else)
	  - ConcHolder: now just a typedef alias for ConcSession
	* factored CHost class out of string_socket.(h|cpp)
	  - moved old CHost::AnswerByRequest() calling context in RunThread() into virtual HandleClientConnection() [for worker-threads]
	  - moved old CHost::AnswerByRequest() to CHost::HandleClientRequest(): handle a single client request [should be worker-local]
	  - factored HandleClientRequest() into GetRequest(), SendResponse(), and HandleSocketError()
	  - report client peer address with CHost errors using new SocketPeer() function [doesn't work for closed sockets of course]
	* factored out QueryResult, CQueryResultIndex from ConcHolder.h to new QueryResult.h
	* added mantis feature-request #661: unified server request protocols
	  - implemented leaf-server commands for branch servers
	  - implemented branch-server commands for leaf servers
	  - allow multiple branch servers in a single process, read from a single ddc_server.cfg
	    + final field of ddc_server.cfg lines (CHost::m_LocalPath) is read as label of parent branch-server
	    + documented ddc_*.cfg syntax as ddc_cfg(5)
	* new abstract DDCTime object
	  - new configure option --enable-hires-clock (enabled by default only if --enable-debug)
	  - TODO: use this consistently wherever timeouts come into play
	* re-worked logging framework
	  - new log-levels ddcLL* (None,Error,Warn,Info,Debug,Trace) a la Log::Log4perl
	    + backwards-compatible aliases pdWeakDensity etc. should work as expected
	  - new global log-level ddcLogLevel
	  - new global log-level-sensitive wrapper macros ddcLogTrace() etc.
	  - new ddcLog() function replaces concord_daemon_log() [with back-compatible wrapper]
	  - use global lock for log access
	  - use log-levels in ConcordOptions.cpp: suppress verbose echo of options at log levels < debug
	* moved Format(...) into ddcString.(h|cpp)
	  - new variable-argument version vFormat(format, va_list)
	* re-factored CommonLib stuff from src/common/ into src/CommonLib/
	  - eliminate ugly 1-liner CommonLib/*.cpp hacks
	* added and documented new server-options file $RML/etc/ddc_server.opt
	  - report active server options in ddc_daemon on server startup

