v2.0.43 Thu, 02 Jun 2016 14:30:01 +0200 moocow
	+ fixed mantis bug #14812: allow truncated-symbol searches for integer-symbols
	  - lexer wart: (19*) was being scanned as ('19' && '*') rather than ('19'*)
	+ added 'WITHOR' operator
	+ added lexer aliases &=, |=, != for WITHIN, WITHOR, WITHOUT respectively
	+ re-worked CQueryWith*Node::EvaluateWithoutHits() to preserve token-wise Match-Ids when in use
	  - allows us to track matching criteria in combination with WITHOR, e.g.
	    ( $p=ADJ* &= ($l=/(?:erst|zweit|dritt)e?$/=2 |= $w=/^[0-9]+\.$/=3) #sep )
	    assigns matchid=2 to $l-conditition matches and matchid=3 to $w-condition matches
	  - match-id =2 no longer clobbers =1 in WITHOUT queries (X=1 without Y=2)
	  - match-id handling should be basically compatible for WITH queries
	+ updated & tidied up querydoc

v2.0.42 Wed, 27 Apr 2016 15:20:52 +0200 moocow
	+ fixed unintuitive results for "count(... #join) #by[$...]" queries (mantis bug #13773)
	  - example (kern): count(* #in s) #by[$p,date/10] -->  "90	$.	1900"
	  - problem was that CQCount::CountLocal() only counted each break exactly once (1st token)
	    which means the above was equivalent to "count($.=0 #in s) #by[...]"
	  - fix uses new CQCountKeyExpr::EvaluateOccurrence() method to iterate over all match tokens
	    on a per-break basis, adding at most 1 to counts for each (key,break) pair
	+ disabled non-POSIX alloca.h dependency in src/common/utf8xx.cpp
	  - only needed by u8_vprintf() and u8_printf(), which we don't use here.
	+ documented ddc_dump --full --tabs format in doc/ddc_tabs.pod (-> ddc_tabs(5))

v2.0.41 Mon, 15 Feb 2016 10:40:21 +0100 moocow
	+ fixed memory leak introduced in v2.0.38 by ddcObject base class
	  - forgot (virtual) destructor ~ddcObject(), caused leaks especially for count() queries
	  - leaks were reported by valgrind in e.g.
	    at 0x4C29180: operator new(unsigned long) (vg_replace_malloc.c:324)
	    ...
	    by 0x440A68: std::set<int, std::less<int>, std::allocator<int> >::insert(int const&) (stl_set.h:502)
            by 0x443776: std::_Rb_tree<int, int, std::_Identity<int>, std::less<int>, std::allocator<int> >::_M_insert_unique(int const&) (stl_tree.h:1503)
	    by 0x43798A: CConcXml::CFreeBiblStringIndex::GetFilterValues(CDDCFilterWithBounds&, std::string const&) const (Bibliography.cpp:544)
	    ...
	  - when parsing ddc-hist count()-queries such as:
	    count(effektiv|www #sep  #has[textClass,/^(?:Belletristik|Gebrauchsliteratur|Wissenschaft|Zeitung)\b/]) #by[date/1,textClass~s/:.*//]
	+ fixed some valgrind-complaints about mismatched new[]/delete()
	+ suppress log messages for "short" requests (status,vstatus,info,vinfo,version) in "weak" branch server log-mode

