v2.0.38 Wed, 20 May 2015 15:22:49 +0200 moocow
	+ CQFContextSort::toString() fix for nontrivial match-ids
	+ added common/ddcObject.h : common base class ddcObject
	  - user data void *m_User (for perl wrappers)
	  - stringification method toString()
	  - json stringification methods toJson(), jsonClass(), jsonData()
	  - object substructure methods Children(), DisownChildren(), Descendants(), Traverse(), TraverseConst()
	    * for future use in perl-wrappers (better reference counting)
	+ re-factored CQuery, CQFilter, CQueryOptions, CQueryCompiler into ddcObject
	+ updated lexer regex for '#cntxt' keyword to (?i:\#(co?n?te?xt?|n)) [was: (?i:\#(cntxt|n))]
	+ complex extra-sentential hit tokens in json mode (no longer simple strings)
	  - disabled by default, can be enabled by configure option --disable-json-deep-context
	+ CQCount::m_keys is now a pointer, for better perl wrapper integration
	+ re-added indexName tracking to CQTokAny (helpful for DiaCollo parsing, doesn't hurt ddc)
	+ added optional lower- and upper-bound arguments to count()-query sort operators #(ASC|DESC)_BY_(KEY|COUNT)
	  - caveat numerator: these apply on a per-subcorpus basis; could be problematic for sparse counts across many subcorpora
	+ re-factored count-query evaluation from ConcHolder.(h|cpp) into QCount.(h|cpp)
	  - removed some redundant CQueryResult fields from CConcHolder (m_SortOrder, m_bSortByString)
	+ re-factored CConcHolder::GetHits(): added variant for pre-parsed queries
	+ removed implicit space-separation in CQCountKeyExprList; we already have globalCountKeyDelim=\002, which is ugly but more useful
	+ fixed bug setting Result.m_AllHitsCount in ConvertCountsToHits()
	  - we were getting m_AllHitsCount=512 (== Limit == m_pIndexator->m_MaxCachedHitsCount) for subcorpora with more "real" count-hits
	+ added keys() query type: extract tuples to query from a count()-query
	  - pretty ugly: it needs to evaluate the count()-query in CQKeys::Compile() in order to generate a proxy query
	    (in general CQWith-conjunction of CQTokSet queries)
	  - currently over-generates, since the key attributes are queried independently
	+ removed bogus leading globalCountKeyDelim and extraneous space after delimiters in count-key hit-ids
	  - added #define DDC_COUNT_KEY_COMPAT in ConcCommon.h for compatibility during transition to v2.0.38
	  - hit-ids reported by CConcHolder::GetCountIds() contained bogus delimiters and spaces prior to v2.0.38
	  - this behavior is retained in v2.0.38 by a compatibility hack, but keys are stored internally without the leading spaces (for keys() queries)
          - compatibility code in CDDCBranchServer::GetFirstHitsFromCorpora() accepts IDs either with or without leading spaces
	  - maintains both ((leaf <v2.0.38) + (branch >=v2.0.38)) and ((leaf >=v2.0.38) + (branch <v2.0.38)) are valid server setups
	  - when all servers are running compatibility hacks (>=v2.0.38), CConcHolder::GetCountIds() hacks can be removed and hit-ids without spaces can be returned
	  - when all servers are returning non-bogus count-key hit-ids, hacks in CDDCBranchServer::GetFirstHitsFromCorpora() can be removed
	+ added m_MatchId field to CQWith and CQueryWithNode: WITH-level match-id clobbers daughters
	  - re-worked match-id handling to use GetMatchId(), SetMatchId()
	+ link in common/(utilit|string_socket).(h|cpp) via CommonLib/libDDCCommon.la
	+ build and install libDDCPCRE.la so that sources get copied properly (annoying)
	+ added some 1-liner proxy src/*/FILE.cpp files containing only #include "../common/FILE.cpp"
	  - fixes automake 'distclean' failures as called by 'distcheck', but is really quite annoying

