	+ set default matchid=255 if any explicit IDs were assigned; else defaults to backwards-compatible id=1
	+ implemented match-id references for context-sort operators #left, #right, #middle
	+ first-stab implementation of token-attribute references in count-by clauses (still expensive and quite slow)
	+ fixed near() wart allowing sub-expressions to match exactly the same token(s)
	  - e.g. near(Sohn,$p=NN,1) returned among other things every hit for (Sohn with $p=NN)
	+ fixed near() bug resulting in inappropriate match-id assignments
	  - problem was missing m_OccurrenceMatchIds.clear() in CQueryNode::ClearAndReserveOccurrences()
	+ added breakstart_ to DEBUG_HIT_JSON output (CTokenNo of first token in the matched sentence)
	+ improved period-local evaluation for anchor ($.) and universal (*) queries (fixed mantis bug #716)
	  - eliminates need for CStringIndexator::RestrictOccurrencesToSearchPeriod() hack
	+ removed special lexer-token MATCHID, since it was interfering with integer-valued index terms (e.g. $page=42)
	+ moved count() evaluation back into search-period loop
	  - attempt to avoid memory explosion by restricting count target-hit generation to inner period-local hits only
	+ added ddc_dump -tabs mode; direct export to TT-like format with special "%%$DDC:BREAK" and "%%$DDC:meta" comments
	+ optimized evaluation for * sub-queries in near()/2, near()/3, and WITH
	+ renamed CQNearEvalItem to more abstract CQOccurrenceIterator, moved to header file QueryNode.h
	+ added option AllowCountByTokenAttributes (default=true)
	+ added #SAMPLE[N] option for count() queries: control subquery sample size
	+ added #ASC_KEY, #DESC_KEY, #ASC_COUNT, #DESC_COUNT sort operators for count() queries

